{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>My father</b> — although He rides upon the steppes, as it says: \"For HaShem is high but He sees the lowly,\" and He is the orphan who has no helper and has not even understanding, and thus in the Torah: \"For HaShem your Elohim is Elohim of gods,\" and after it: \"who executes justice for orphan and widow.\"" "<b>And the meaning of \"in His holy habitation\"</b> — even though His glory's place is on high, and orphans are at the very bottom, which is the earth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:04.664888581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}